WEBVTT

00:00:02.590 --> 00:00:04.170
Summer grasses grow,

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.590
leaving but the dreams of the

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:07.220
long-gone warriors.

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:11.920
The dream of unifying Japan was held 
by many lords of the warring states.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:15.510
Shingen Takeda.

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:17.910
Kenshin Uesugi.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:19.910
Nobunaga Oda.

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:25.670
And finally, one man had attained that dream...

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:27.410
Hideyoshi Toyotomi.

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.320
Japan had been unified,

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:32.050
and a time of peace appeared to be at hand.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.190
However,

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:40.370
Hideyoshi's death cast the land 
back into a maelstrom.

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:44.900
With Ieyasu Tokugawa growing 
more influential by the day,

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:48.850
Mitsunari Ishida tried to prevent his rise to power.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.170
In order to settle their score once and for all,

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:55.350
the two marched their armies to Sekigahara.

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:00.280
Having separated and gone their own ways,

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:03.620
the Sanada brothers faced off again

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:06.500
amidst a massive siege of Ueda Castle

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:09.520
led by Hidetada Tokugawa.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.070
Nobuyuki...

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:51.960
I shall protect you, no matter what.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:58.370
Brother!

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:01.820
Yukimura.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:07.660
You must run, Lord Hidetada.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:11.170
Brother, please stand aside!

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:13.170
I'm afraid I can't.

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:16.300
Then I'll have to force my way through!

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:32.600
Aizu-Wakamatsu Castle

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:36.110
Yonezawa Castle

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:35.890
While Yukimura squared off 
against Hidetada's forces,

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:38.560
Kanetsugu, too, was in the midst of

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:40.440
Hasedo Castle

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:42.430
a fierce battle in Northern Aizu 
against Oshu's Masamune Date.

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:06.040
Just you wait, Mitsunari!

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:10.850
Meanwhile, with Sekigahara 
covered in a dense fog,

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:14.600
thousands of soldiers lay in wait

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:18.360
for the imminent signal to commence warfare.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:29.620
Mt. Sasao

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:29.620
Mt. Matsuo

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:29.620
Sekigahara

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:29.620
Mt. Momokubari

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:21.380
The Eastern Army, led by Ieyasu Tokugawa,

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:25.090
put Masanori Fukushima and 
Kiyomasa Kato on their front lines,

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:28.070
leaving Ieyasu's main unit in the rear.

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:29.620
This was a "flying wedge formation."

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:46.720
Mt. Sasao

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:46.720
Mt. Matsuo

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:46.720
Sekigahara

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:46.720
Mt. Momokubari

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:38.320
On the other hand, Mitsunari Ishida's Western Army

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:40.530
deployed its main force at Mt. Sasao,

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:44.970
with troops on both flanks bidding 
to surround the enemy.

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:46.720
This was an "inverted wedge formation."

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:51.450
With the numerical advantage created 
by Yukimura stalling Hidetada's forces

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:55.240
and a formation that fully utilized 
his geographical superiority,

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:59.850
Mitsunari's preparations to defeat 
Ieyasu were complete.

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:03.990
How much longer?

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:06.380
I'm sick of waiting here.

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:08.240
Settle down, Masanori.

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:11.740
Lord Ieyasu's waiting for this fog to lift.

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:16.000
But while we're sitting here, 
the enemy might attack us!

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:17.610
Wait for the signal.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:21.250
Lord Ieyasu has left the vanguard in our hands.

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:24.200
No matter what happens, we'll be 
the ones to draw first blood.

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:26.760
Huh?

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:38.020
Is that...

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:42.700
Naomasa?

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.530
That sneaky bastard!

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:49.390
<i>This is Tokugawa's war.</i>

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:51.800
<i>I'm not about to let Hideyoshi's lapdogs</i>

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:53.790
<i>hog all the glory!</i>

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:57.260
So Naomasa did charge in, after all.

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:03.300
What?

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:08.870
I am the Tokugawa Army's Naomasa Ii,

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:10.980
and I shall land the first strike!

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:19.560
R-Red armor?

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:22.250
It's Ii's Red Devil!

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:26.750
It's time.

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:28.990
All troops, advance!

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:33.280
There's the signal.

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:36.830
Finally... I thought I was gonna explode.

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:38.580
Charge!

00:06:41.390 --> 00:06:42.330
Not yet.

00:06:42.780 --> 00:06:44.090
Hold your positions.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:54.100
Fire the cannons!

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:08.370
Cannons?

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:12.710
Damn, he's using cannons!

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:14.160
Don't break formation!

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:26.670
Mt. Sasao

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:26.670
Mt. Matsuo

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:26.670
Sekigahara

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:26.670
Mt. Momokubari

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:17.490
The Eastern Army had begun their advance,

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:20.990
but the artillery fire forced 
them to run for cover.

00:07:20.990 --> 00:07:22.860
When their formation began to fall apart,

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:24.950
the Western Army surrounded them on both flanks,

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:26.670
and commenced a pincer attack.

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:28.760
Charge!

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:41.180
Surround them and finish them off.

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:44.760
<i>Kobayakawa...</i>

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:54.140
So far, so good.

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:57.120
Our army's at a disadvantage.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:00.610
The cannons' delay in arrival is really hurting us.

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:17.970
Run away, Lord Hidetada!

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:19.440
R-Right.

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:27.900
Ueda Castle is the Sanada clan's home!

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:31.150
I shall protect it from any and all attacks!

00:08:31.420 --> 00:08:35.410
I won't retreat from the path I've chosen, either!

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:37.160
Brother!

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:50.430
Our cannon fire has thrown the enemy into chaos.

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:54.010
Their command chain's broken, so they 
aren't putting up much of a fight.

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:58.000
With their escape routes blocked by 
the inverted wedge formation,

00:08:58.000 --> 00:08:59.930
our allies are taking them out, one after the other.

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:04.120
<i>This battle mustn't be allowed to drag on.</i>

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:07.900
<i>We must settle things while Yukimura 
stalls the other troops.</i>

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:10.290
We're going for the kill.

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:12.190
Inform Kobayakawa.

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:13.240
Yes, sir!

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:28.330
Mt. Sasao

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:28.330
Mt. Matsuo

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:28.330
Sekigahara

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:28.330
Mt. Momokubari

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:21.550
The Western Army, while attacking their 
surrounded enemies relentlessly,

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:23.820
looked to finish things in one fell swoop

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:28.330
by sending Kobayakawa's unit, on Mt. 
Matsuo, the signal to move out.

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:32.840
<i>Will Kobayakawa make his move?</i>

00:09:35.690 --> 00:09:38.090
The Western Army camp 
has fired a smoke signal.

00:09:42.590 --> 00:09:44.620
Be sure to keep them surrounded.

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:45.850
Lord Yoshitsugu?

00:09:46.190 --> 00:09:47.560
I'm moving out.

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:48.980
There is something I must do.

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:55.670
<i>I knew it. He was allied with Tokugawa.</i>

00:09:57.850 --> 00:09:59.990
Kobayakawa's unit is not moving!

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:08.730
<i>Ieyasu set me up...</i>

00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:11.230
Lord Otani's going to confront him!

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:15.010
You planned this?

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:20.380
Yes, but we still don't know if he'll do our bidding.

00:10:21.110 --> 00:10:24.010
Nor how this war will turn out.

00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:54.380
What are you doing, Lord Hidetada?

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:55.250
Fire!

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:09.680
Wh-What's going on?

00:11:12.590 --> 00:11:13.690
Fall back!

00:11:14.470 --> 00:11:16.550
Now's our chance.

00:11:16.550 --> 00:11:17.610
All units, retreat!

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:27.580
<i>The castle!</i>

00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:31.360
Lord Yukimura...

00:11:54.250 --> 00:11:56.100
Ii's Red Devil,

00:11:56.100 --> 00:11:59.860
this is as far as you go.

00:12:00.310 --> 00:12:02.610
You seem too injured to stop me, though.

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:05.490
I think this is the perfect handicap.

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:09.620
En garde!

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:16.420
I see now.

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:17.990
What's up?

00:12:18.470 --> 00:12:20.420
Mitsunari's only using the cannons to intimidate.

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:25.430
That fool's deliberately firing away from the soldiers.

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:27.940
Ha, how soft.

00:12:27.940 --> 00:12:29.430
But it's just like him.

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:31.860
Let's go break his face, Masanori.

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:32.910
Yeah!

00:12:34.130 --> 00:12:36.670
Enemy at twelve o'clock, heading our way!

00:12:37.270 --> 00:12:39.330
Kiyomasa, Masanori...

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:40.690
They're coming.

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:42.910
My lord, we must hold them off.

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:45.170
How about firing the cannons at them?

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:46.200
I know.

00:12:47.360 --> 00:12:48.440
<i>I have to attack them.</i>

00:12:49.970 --> 00:12:50.590
My lord!

00:12:50.590 --> 00:12:51.650
My lord!

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:55.700
Lure them in,

00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:57.460
and wait for my orders.

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:05.220
Yoshitsugu!

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:10.710
You won't pass.

00:13:13.940 --> 00:13:15.600
I knew I'd run into you.

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:21.950
Curse you, Sanada!

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:26.610
Our goal isn't to defeat the 
Sanada clan, but Mitsunari.

00:13:27.390 --> 00:13:30.970
If we hurry to Sekigahara and aid Lord Ieyasu,

00:13:30.970 --> 00:13:32.870
the land will be brought under one rule.

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:34.870
Oh, shut up.

00:13:36.070 --> 00:13:37.620
Will we make it in time?

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:39.110
I cannot say.

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:42.660
All we can do is hurry there.

00:13:50.090 --> 00:13:52.750
My lord, we can't let them advance further!

00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:54.140
Your orders, sir!

00:13:55.990 --> 00:13:58.390
Tokugawa's main unit is making its move.

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:18.420
Mt. Sasao

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:18.420
Mt. Matsuo

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:18.420
Sekigahara

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:18.420
Mt. Momokubari

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:03.670
Kiyomasa and Masanori's unit

00:14:03.670 --> 00:14:07.860
was closing in on Mt. Sasao's base, 
where Mitsumoto had set up camp.

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:10.660
Kobayakawa's unit still hadn't moved,

00:14:10.880 --> 00:14:13.250
so Ieyasu moved his own unit out,

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:15.490
in a bid to support his flanked army

00:14:15.490 --> 00:14:18.410
and take control of the see-saw battle.

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:19.920
My lord!

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:23.370
Fire.

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:24.670
At what?

00:14:25.700 --> 00:14:26.670
The soldiers.

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:34.510
He's firing at us now.

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:36.520
Mitsunari!

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:43.080
I'll be on my way.

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:43.770
Yes.

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:53.600
You seriously think Mitsunari will be able to

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:55.800
prevent the Tokugawa clan's rise to power?

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:57.080
You're out of your mind!

00:14:57.590 --> 00:15:03.080
I'm simply fighting for the man 
who's earned my total respect.

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:04.210
<i>What?</i>

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:11.070
Laugh if you must.

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:12.620
But you know,

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:16.850
I don't regret having 
chosen this path for a second.

00:15:17.130 --> 00:15:19.180
Very well... I'll cut you down!

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:49.010
My lord,

00:15:49.990 --> 00:15:53.450
the wind is changing directions...

00:16:11.550 --> 00:16:13.610
It isn't too late!

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:15.990
Join me, Yoshitsugu!

00:16:16.290 --> 00:16:18.700
You ask me now, of all times?

00:16:19.030 --> 00:16:22.940
You know the tide flows Tokugawa's way!

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:24.460
So why?!

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:27.600
I simply wish to learn what I can see

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:30.190
if I go against the flow.

00:16:30.900 --> 00:16:33.970
Then we can't walk side by side anymore?

00:16:34.670 --> 00:16:36.900
This is the path I chose.

00:16:48.990 --> 00:16:49.730
Yoshitsugu!

00:16:59.710 --> 00:17:01.830
Let us chase after our own dreams

00:17:02.510 --> 00:17:04.080
and see where they take us.

00:17:10.730 --> 00:17:12.100
Yoshitsugu!

00:17:13.110 --> 00:17:16.260
We knew it would come to this...

00:17:16.520 --> 00:17:19.370
Forgive me, Mitsunari.

00:17:23.510 --> 00:17:26.520
Is this where your dream led?

00:17:26.890 --> 00:17:29.650
Yoshitsugu!

00:17:36.170 --> 00:17:38.210
That damned Mitsunari!

00:17:40.980 --> 00:17:42.340
Lord Tadakatsu?

00:18:11.510 --> 00:18:13.140
Tadakatsu Honda...

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:14.490
My lord!

00:18:15.970 --> 00:18:18.280
Kobayakawa has turned on us!

00:18:19.710 --> 00:18:20.530
My lord!

00:18:21.260 --> 00:18:23.530
Both the Otani and Shima units were wiped out.

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:47.310
Mt. Sasao

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:47.310
Mt. Matsuo

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:47.310
Sekigahara

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:47.310
Mt. Momokubari

00:18:34.970 --> 00:18:37.250
The loss of Yoshitsugu and Sakon caused

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:40.150
the Western Army's inverted wedge 
formation to fall apart.

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:44.560
And when Kanetsugu began marching 
toward Mitsunari's camp,

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:47.310
the battle was decided.

00:19:02.830 --> 00:19:05.580
<i>I shall be the one to protect the Toyotomi clan!</i>

00:19:16.850 --> 00:19:18.020
Mitsunari!

00:19:18.530 --> 00:19:20.340
This battle is already over!

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:22.550
Mind your own business!

00:19:42.930 --> 00:19:44.820
I'm not finished yet!

00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:53.580
Ieyasu!

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:11.310
Lord Yukimura!

00:20:11.860 --> 00:20:14.850
Lord Nobuyuki is here, 
with Tokugawa troops in tow!

00:20:15.350 --> 00:20:16.360
What?!

00:20:20.350 --> 00:20:22.260
Why did you return?

00:20:22.980 --> 00:20:25.000
We shall stand with Lord Mitsunari to the last—

00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:26.510
The war is over.

00:20:27.680 --> 00:20:29.370
Mitsunari was defeated.

00:20:29.560 --> 00:20:31.270
Th-That can't be.

00:20:31.870 --> 00:20:33.340
I don't believe you!

00:20:33.340 --> 00:20:34.620
He was defeated!

00:20:35.370 --> 00:20:38.130
That we stand here should be proof enough.

00:20:40.140 --> 00:20:41.550
Th-Then...

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:43.380
Did Lord Mitsunari...

00:21:01.910 --> 00:21:05.040
Ieyasu...

00:21:25.860 --> 00:21:26.910
Mitsunari...

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:31.190
There may be people who complain about you.

00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:35.100
But I understand you better than anyone.

00:21:39.990 --> 00:21:41.370
<i>Lord Hideyoshi...</i>

00:21:52.920 --> 00:21:57.350
Lord Mitsunari!

00:22:04.960 --> 00:22:09.890
<i>Episode 4</i>

00:22:04.960 --> 00:22:09.890
<i>The Sekigahara Sunset</i>

00:23:41.890 --> 00:23:45.150
Sengoku Musou 
High School

00:23:41.890 --> 00:23:45.150
4th Period

00:23:46.330 --> 00:23:47.650
<i>I shall go against the flow.</i>

00:23:47.650 --> 00:23:49.150
Tokugawa Electronics

00:24:05.470 --> 00:24:06.450
<i>This is strange.</i>

00:24:06.840 --> 00:24:08.920
Tokugawa Electronics

00:24:07.620 --> 00:24:08.590
<i>How?</i>

00:24:08.920 --> 00:24:09.880
<i>To Be Continued</i>

00:24:09.880 --> 00:24:24.800
<i>Next Episode</i>

00:24:10.580 --> 00:24:14.800
The next story is Yukimura's life-or-death trial.

00:24:14.800 --> 00:24:16.140
Amidst the voices crying for blood

00:24:16.410 --> 00:24:17.970
and those begging for mercy,

00:24:18.350 --> 00:24:21.670
what kind of decision will Nobuyuki make?

00:24:21.480 --> 00:24:24.800
<i>Episode Five 
The Destination of Life</i>

00:24:22.010 --> 00:24:24.600
Next time: "The Destination of Life."
